{
  "runId": "mq2xne1w-idvqyb",
  "workflowName": "findings_to_html_v2",
  "script": "export const meta = {\n  name: 'findings_to_html_v2',\n  description: 'Render FINDINGS.md into a self-contained HTML page via parallel section authors plus a synthesizer that writes the file to disk.',\n  phases: [\n    { title: 'Section authors' },\n    { title: 'Assemble and write HTML' }\n  ]\n};\n\nphase('Section authors');\n\nconst sourceNote = `Read the source report at: ${args.sourcePath}\\nUse your Read tool. Use ONLY content that exists in that file — do not invent recommendations, numbers, or quotes.`;\n\nconst styleNote = `Output an HTML BODY-FRAGMENT only. No <html>, <head>, <body>, <style>, <script> tags. Use semantic HTML5. Class hooks the assembler expects:\n- section wrapper: <section class=\"block\" id=\"...\">\n- recommendation card: <article class=\"rec\">\n- card header bar: <header class=\"rec__head\"> with .rec__rank, .rec__title, badges\n- definition list inside card: <dl class=\"rec__meta\">\n- metric tile: <div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"metric__val\">…</div><div class=\"metric__lbl\">…</div></div> inside <div class=\"metric-grid\">\n- badges: <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">0.NN</span>, badge--high / badge--med / badge--low\n- call-out: <aside class=\"callout\">\n- inline code: <code>, muted text: <span class=\"muted\">\nKeep prose tight. No emojis. No external resources.`;\n\nconst sectionPrompts = [\n  {\n    label: 'hero+metrics',\n    focus: `Emit exactly one <section class=\"block\" id=\"hero\"> containing:\n1. <header class=\"page-head\"> with <h1>${args.title}</h1>, <p class=\"lede\">${args.subtitle}</p>, then a paragraph: \"${args.headline}\"\n2. A short method paragraph (2-3 sentences) summarizing: analyze.js walks 385 jsonl sessions; an evidence pack is fed to a 6-specialist parallel workflow + synthesizer; ranking = impact x confidence / effort with cross-specialist deduplication. Pull phrasing from the source's Method paragraph.\n3. <div class=\"metric-grid\"> containing one <div class=\"metric\"> per item, in this order: ${JSON.stringify(args.metrics)}.`\n  },\n  {\n    label: 'top10',\n    focus: `Emit exactly one <section class=\"block\" id=\"top10\"> with <h2>Top recommendations (ranked, confidence-scored)</h2> followed by 10 <article class=\"rec\"> blocks (in source order) for items 1..10 in the source's \"Top recommendations\" section.\nFor each card:\n<article class=\"rec\">\n  <header class=\"rec__head\">\n    <span class=\"rec__rank\">#N</span>\n    <h3 class=\"rec__title\">TITLE</h3>\n    <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">conf 0.NN</span>\n    <span class=\"badge badge--high|med|low\">impact: TIER</span>\n    <span class=\"badge badge--high|med|low\">effort: TIER</span>\n  </header>\n  <dl class=\"rec__meta\">\n    <dt>Evidence</dt><dd>…short evidence sentence from source…</dd>\n    <dt>Action</dt><dd>…concrete action…</dd>\n    <dt>Expected outcome</dt><dd>…outcome…</dd>\n  </dl>\n</article>\nMap impact/effort strings: high→badge--high, medium→badge--med, low→badge--low.`\n  },\n  {\n    label: 'tier2+usage',\n    focus: `Emit TWO sections back-to-back (no extra wrapper):\n1. <section class=\"block\" id=\"second-tier\"><h2>Second tier (ship after telemetry makes them measurable)</h2><ul class=\"tier2\">…</ul></section> — one <li> per item in source's \"Second tier\" section. Each li: bold the rec title, then a <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">0.NN</span>, then a single-sentence rationale in <span class=\"muted\">…</span>.\n2. <section class=\"block\" id=\"usage\"><h2>What I (the user) should do differently</h2><ol class=\"usage\">…</ol></section> — one <li> per item in source's user-side section. Each li: bold an imperative title, then one sentence of rationale.`\n  },\n  {\n    label: 'meta+artifacts',\n    focus: `Emit exactly one <section class=\"block\" id=\"meta\"> with:\n1. <h2>Meta-notes &amp; artifacts</h2>\n2. <aside class=\"callout\"><ul>…</ul></aside> — bullet list of the source's \"Meta-notes / what would tighten this further\" items, tightened slightly for HTML.\n3. <h3>Artifacts</h3><ul class=\"artifacts\">…</ul> — one <li> per artifact (analyze.js, sessions_summary.json, aggregate.json, evidence_pack.md, FINDINGS.md) with the source's one-line description; wrap filenames in <code>.\n4. <footer class=\"run\">Workflow run: pi_sessions_optimization · 7 agents · 392,566 tokens · $2.89.</footer>`\n  }\n];\n\nconst fragSchema = {\n  type: 'object',\n  required: ['htmlFragment'],\n  properties: { htmlFragment: { type: 'string' }, notes: { type: 'string' } }\n};\n\nconst fragments = await parallel(sectionPrompts.map(p => () => agent(\n  `${sourceNote}\\n\\n${p.focus}\\n\\n${styleNote}`,\n  { label: p.label, tier: 'medium', schema: fragSchema }\n)));\n\nconst labeled = sectionPrompts.map((p, i) => ({\n  label: p.label,\n  ok: !!fragments[i]?.htmlFragment,\n  html: fragments[i]?.htmlFragment || ''\n}));\nlog(`fragments returned ok: ${labeled.filter(x => x.ok).length}/${labeled.length}`);\n\nphase('Assemble and write HTML');\n\n// Keep CSS as a JS string the assembler can paste verbatim\nconst css = String.raw`\n:root{--bg:#0b0d10;--bg-elev:#14181d;--bg-card:#181d23;--border:#232a33;--text:#e6edf3;--text-dim:#9aa7b4;--text-mute:#6b7785;--accent:#7cc4ff;--accent-2:#a3e6b1;--warn:#ffb86b;--conf:#b794f4;--code-bg:#0f1318;--radius:10px;--radius-sm:6px;--maxw:980px;--mono:ui-monospace,\"SF Mono\",Menlo,Consolas,monospace;--sans:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,\"Inter\",\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,sans-serif}\n@media (prefers-color-scheme: light){:root{--bg:#fafbfc;--bg-elev:#fff;--bg-card:#fff;--border:#e5e9ee;--text:#1a1f26;--text-dim:#4a5562;--text-mute:#7b8593;--accent:#0969da;--accent-2:#1a7f37;--warn:#9a6700;--conf:#7e3ce8;--code-bg:#f6f8fa}}\n*{box-sizing:border-box}\nhtml,body{margin:0;padding:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--text);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased}\n.page{max-width:var(--maxw);margin:0 auto;padding:48px 24px 96px}\nh1,h2,h3{font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.01em;line-height:1.25}\nh1{font-size:34px;margin:0 0 8px}\nh2{font-size:22px;margin:0 0 16px;padding-bottom:10px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}\nh3{font-size:16px;margin:0}\np{margin:0 0 14px;color:var(--text-dim)}\ncode{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.88em;background:var(--code-bg);padding:1px 6px;border-radius:4px;border:1px solid var(--border)}\nstrong{color:var(--text)}\nem{color:var(--text-dim);font-style:italic}\n.lede{font-size:17px;color:var(--text-dim);margin:0 0 18px}\n.block{background:var(--bg-elev);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:28px;margin:0 0 24px}\n.metric-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(150px,1fr));gap:10px;margin-top:18px}\n.metric{background:var(--bg-card);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius-sm);padding:12px 14px}\n.metric__val{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:17px;font-weight:600;color:var(--text);letter-spacing:-.02em}\n.metric__lbl{font-size:11px;color:var(--text-mute);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em;margin-top:4px}\n.rec{background:var(--bg-card);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius-sm);padding:18px 20px;margin:0 0 14px}\n.rec__head{display:flex;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;margin-bottom:12px}\n.rec__rank{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;color:var(--text-mute);background:var(--bg);padding:2px 8px;border-radius:999px;border:1px solid var(--border)}\n.rec__title{flex:1 1 auto;min-width:200px;font-size:16px;color:var(--text)}\n.rec__meta{margin:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:130px 1fr;gap:6px 16px;font-size:14px}\n.rec__meta dt{color:var(--text-mute);font-size:12px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em;padding-top:2px}\n.rec__meta dd{margin:0;color:var(--text-dim)}\n.badge{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:999px;border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text-dim);background:var(--bg);white-space:nowrap}\n.badge--conf{color:var(--conf)}\n.badge--high{color:var(--accent-2)}\n.badge--med{color:var(--warn)}\n.badge--low{color:var(--text-mute)}\nul,ol{margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px;color:var(--text-dim)}\nli{margin-bottom:6px}\nli strong{color:var(--text)}\n.tier2 li{margin-bottom:10px}\n.muted{color:var(--text-mute);font-size:13px}\n.callout{background:var(--bg-card);border-left:3px solid var(--accent);border-radius:var(--radius-sm);padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 18px}\n.callout ul{margin:0}\n.artifacts code{background:var(--bg)}\n.run{margin-top:24px;padding-top:16px;border-top:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text-mute);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px}\n@media (max-width:640px){.page{padding:24px 14px 64px}.rec__meta{grid-template-columns:1fr}.rec__meta dt{padding-top:8px}h1{font-size:26px}}\n`;\n\nconst synthSchema = {\n  type: 'object',\n  required: ['ok'],\n  properties: {\n    ok: { type: 'boolean' },\n    bytesWritten: { type: 'number' },\n    path: { type: 'string' },\n    notes: { type: 'string' }\n  }\n};\n\nconst synthPrompt = `Build ONE self-contained HTML document by concatenating the four fragments below into this shell, then WRITE it to ${args.outputPath} using your Write tool.\n\nSHELL (replace <!--FRAGMENTS--> with the four fragments in order, separated by a single newline):\n\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>${args.title}</title>\n<style>${css}</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"page\">\n<!--FRAGMENTS-->\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>\n\nFRAGMENTS (verbatim, ordered):\n${labeled.map((f, i) => `==== fragment[${i}] label=${f.label} ok=${f.ok} ====\\n${f.html}`).join('\\n\\n')}\n\nRULES:\n1. Do not modify fragment content except to strip any stray <html>/<head>/<body>/<style>/<script> tags that leaked into them.\n2. If a fragment is empty or has no <section>, replace its slot with <section class=\"block\"><h2>Section unavailable</h2><p class=\"muted\">Author returned no content.</p></section>.\n3. No external assets. No analytics.\n4. Final document MUST begin with <!DOCTYPE html> and contain exactly one <html>, <head>, <body>, <style>.\n5. Call your Write tool with path=\"${args.outputPath}\" and the full HTML as content.\n6. Return JSON { ok: true, bytesWritten: <number>, path: \"${args.outputPath}\" }.`;\n\nconst synth = await agent(synthPrompt, { label: 'html assembler', tier: 'big', schema: synthSchema });\n\nreturn {\n  ok: !!synth?.ok,\n  path: args.outputPath,\n  bytesWritten: synth?.bytesWritten || 0,\n  fragmentResults: labeled.map(f => ({ label: f.label, ok: f.ok, bytes: f.html.length })),\n  synthNotes: synth?.notes || null\n};",
  "args": "{\n\"outputPath\": \"/Users/anishthite/workspace/pi-lookback/FINDINGS.html\",\n\"sourcePath\": \"/Users/anishthite/workspace/pi-lookback/FINDINGS.md\",\n\"title\": \"Pi sessions look-back — findings & ranked optimizations\",\n\"subtitle\": \"385 sessions · 1.22 B tokens · $1,951 · workflow-driven analysis\",\n\"headline\": \"Pi's standing orders work as documentation but lose to tempo at decision time. Fixes that move rules from prose to runtime gates dominate the top tier.\",\n\"metrics\": [\n  {\"label\": \"Sessions analyzed\", \"value\": \"385\"},\n  {\"label\": \"Total tokens\", \"value\": \"1.22 B\"},\n  {\"label\": \"Total spend\", \"value\": \"$1,951.00\"},\n  {\"label\": \"Tool calls\", \"value\": \"14,851\"},\n  {\"label\": \"Tool errors\", \"value\": \"581 (3.91%)\"},\n  {\"label\": \"Failed-retry loops\", \"value\": \"681\"},\n  {\"label\": \"Dup-arg replays\", \"value\": \"537\"},\n  {\"label\": \"Parallel / serial ratio\", \"value\": \"0.127\"},\n  {\"label\": \"workflow tool calls\", \"value\": \"0 / 385\"},\n  {\"label\": \"subagent in sessions\", \"value\": \"18% (target >30%)\"},\n  {\"label\": \"async subagent share\", \"value\": \"11%\"},\n  {\"label\": \"p99 / max tool calls\", \"value\": \"258 / 414\"},\n  {\"label\": \"claude-opus-4-7 share\", \"value\": \"94%\"},\n  {\"label\": \"p99 / max cost / session\", \"value\": \"$47.88 / $106.19\"}\n]\n}",
  "sessionId": "019e9d8f-62be-7d8b-878b-8168c2449d6e",
  "journal": [
    {
      "index": 2,
      "hash": "d07b6f81f764f1f8b084cfea58a3c720467395897d59f9c06c14600f7b29c43e",
      "result": {
        "htmlFragment": "<section class=\"block\" id=\"second-tier\"><h2>Second tier (ship after telemetry makes them measurable)</h2><ul class=\"tier2\"><li><span class=\"muted\">Source report path was <code>undefined</code>; no second-tier items could be read.</span></li></ul></section><section class=\"block\" id=\"usage\"><h2>What I (the user) should do differently</h2><ol class=\"usage\"><li><span class=\"muted\">Source report path was <code>undefined</code>; no user-side recommendations could be read.</span></li></ol></section>",
        "notes": "Source report path provided to this subagent was the literal string \"undefined\" — no file to read. Emitted placeholder sections with the expected class hooks so the assembler does not break; please re-run with a valid source path."
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "hash": "fb525465e377d93f5fc6932c82367884115ad3ee8780e79b258023881937f32f",
      "result": {
        "htmlFragment": "<section class=\"block\" id=\"meta\">\n  <h2>Meta-notes &amp; artifacts</h2>\n  <aside class=\"callout\">\n    <ul>\n      <li>The aggregate JSON has per-session rows, but raw user prompts and tool arguments were deliberately not sampled beyond the first 200 chars (privacy posture). A per-task-class breakdown (feature / refactor / debug / conversation) would let us size <span class=\"muted\">#3, #4, #9</span> precisely. Easiest path: cluster the <code>firstUserPrompt</code> field in <code>sessions_summary.json</code> by topic.</li>\n      <li>We do not yet know whether prompt caching is on — <span class=\"muted\">#5</span> collapses to a no-op if it is.</li>\n      <li>90 turns ended with <code>stopReason=\"error\"</code> and 30 with <code>aborted</code>; those are worth a separate pass to see if they cluster on specific tools or models.</li>\n      <li>The corpus is 94% <code>claude-opus-4-7</code>. Per-task tiering (Haiku for grep/read fan-out, Sonnet for synthesis, Opus only for judgment) is plausibly the largest single $ cut available <em>after</em> prompt caching is verified, but lacks evidence here.</li>\n    </ul>\n  </aside>\n  <h3>Artifacts</h3>\n  <ul class=\"artifacts\">\n    <li><code>analyze.js</code> — JSONL walker, per-session metric extractor.</li>\n    <li><code>sessions_summary.json</code> (~825 KB) — per-session rows with tool counts, errors, costs, friction signals.</li>\n    <li><code>aggregate.json</code> — cross-corpus rollups, top-N session lists.</li>\n    <li><code>evidence_pack.md</code> — distilled signal pack fed to the workflow.</li>\n    <li><code>FINDINGS.md</code> — the source report file.</li>\n  </ul>\n  <footer class=\"run\">Workflow run: pi_sessions_optimization · 7 agents · 392,566 tokens · $2.89.</footer>\n</section>"
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 0,
      "hash": "aa336f768e3d4206f69f3ed8b615663783c9791fc90f91632248a3eedc20b605",
      "result": {
        "htmlFragment": "<section class=\"block\" id=\"hero\">\n  <header class=\"page-head\">\n    <h1>Pi sessions look-back</h1>\n    <p class=\"lede\">Findings &amp; ranked optimizations across 385 sessions.</p>\n    <p>pi's standing orders work as documentation but lose to tempo at decision time. Fixes that move rules from prose to <em>runtime gates</em> dominate the top tier.</p>\n  </header>\n  <p>Walked all 385 jsonl sessions under <code>~/.pi/agent/sessions</code> (245 MB). Per-session stats were extracted with <code>analyze.js</code> (cost, tool calls, error rates, dup-arg replays, failed retries, parallel/serial batching, orchestration adoption, model usage), with cross-cutting signal distilled into <code>evidence_pack.md</code>. A six-specialist workflow analyzed the pack from cost / orchestration / batching / tool-error / long-session / standing-orders angles; a synthesizer merged duplicates and ranked by impact &times; confidence / effort.</p>\n  <div class=\"metric-grid\">\n    <div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"metric__val\">385</div><div class=\"metric__lbl\">sessions</div></div>\n    <div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"metric__val\">1.22B</div><div class=\"metric__lbl\">tokens</div></div>\n    <div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"metric__val\">$1,951</div><div class=\"metric__lbl\">total spend</div></div>\n    <div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"metric__val\">14,851</div><div class=\"metric__lbl\">tool calls</div></div>\n    <div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"metric__val\">681</div><div class=\"metric__lbl\">failed-retry loops</div></div>\n    <div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"metric__val\">537</div><div class=\"metric__lbl\">dup-arg replays</div></div>\n    <div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"metric__val\">0</div><div class=\"metric__lbl\"><code>workflow</code> calls</div></div>\n    <div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"metric__val\">18%</div><div class=\"metric__lbl\">sessions using subagent</div></div>\n    <div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"metric__val\">11%</div><div class=\"metric__lbl\">sessions using async</div></div>\n    <div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"metric__val\">0.127</div><div class=\"metric__lbl\">parallel / serial ratio</div></div>\n  </div>\n</section>",
        "notes": "Source: FINDINGS.md. Task parameters were \"undefined\" for title, lede, callout paragraph, and metric list — inferred from source headline. Method paragraph paraphrases the source Method paragraph. Metrics drawn verbatim from the \"Corpus headline\" line."
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "hash": "47080b0a2e44865a5717aaff59d9dc8aa7ed97a8c1279cf0c3c3d955c825cc27",
      "result": {
        "htmlFragment": "<section class=\"block\" id=\"top10\">\n  <h2>Top recommendations (ranked, confidence-scored)</h2>\n\n  <article class=\"rec\">\n    <header class=\"rec__head\">\n      <span class=\"rec__rank\">#1</span>\n      <h3 class=\"rec__title\">Failed-retry loop breaker with hypothesis-change gate</h3>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">conf 0.90</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--high\">impact: high</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--low\">effort: low</span>\n    </header>\n    <dl class=\"rec__meta\">\n      <dt>Evidence</dt><dd>681 failed-retry loops corpus-wide (~1.77 / session); largest single waste category. Top offender: <code>test pi chrome</code> session (37 retries, $106, 317 tool calls).</dd>\n      <dt>Action</dt><dd>Per-(tool, target) failure counter. On 3rd deterministic failure (ENOENT, EPERM, syntax, \"not unique\") inject a forced-reasoning turn demanding a new hypothesis or escalation. Transient errors keep free backoff retries.</dd>\n      <dt>Expected outcome</dt><dd>Eliminate the bulk of those 681 loops; conservatively trim 10–20% off tail-session tool-call counts and proportionally cut the p95+ $/session.</dd>\n    </dl>\n  </article>\n\n  <article class=\"rec\">\n    <header class=\"rec__head\">\n      <span class=\"rec__rank\">#2</span>\n      <h3 class=\"rec__title\">Duplicate-arg replay detector + cached inline + escalation</h3>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">conf 0.88</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--high\">impact: high</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--low\">effort: low</span>\n    </header>\n    <dl class=\"rec__meta\">\n      <dt>Evidence</dt><dd>537 exact-replay calls (tool + args byte-identical), concentrated in long sessions — 89/317 in <code>test pi chrome</code>, 77/414 in the implementation-notes loop. Zero new information for non-zero cost.</dd>\n      <dt>Action</dt><dd>Session-scoped LRU keyed by (tool, normalized_args) for idempotent tools (Read, Grep, find_files, ctx_search, ctx_execute_file). 2nd identical call returns cached result with <code>[cached]</code>; 3rd forces a planning turn; 4th escalates to summarize-and-handoff. Bash/network stay non-cacheable.</dd>\n      <dt>Expected outcome</dt><dd>Directly trims input-token spend on the long-session tail; visibly shortens sessions that loop on the same Read/Grep.</dd>\n    </dl>\n  </article>\n\n  <article class=\"rec\">\n    <header class=\"rec__head\">\n      <span class=\"rec__rank\">#3</span>\n      <h3 class=\"rec__title\">PreToolUse orchestration gate on session-first multi-file mutations</h3>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">conf 0.82</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--high\">impact: high</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--med\">effort: medium</span>\n    </header>\n    <dl class=\"rec__meta\">\n      <dt>Evidence</dt><dd><code>workflow</code> calls = 0/385. <code>subagent</code> used in 18% of sessions (AGENTS.md floor: &gt;30%). Cross-corpus subagent / (write+edit+bash) = 0.035 — 10× under the explicit floor. Prose loses to conversational tempo.</dd>\n      <dt>Action</dt><dd>Extension hook <code>orchestration-gate</code>: when the first Write/Edit/Bash-mutate of a session touches &gt;1 directory or creates &gt;1 new file AND prior subagent dispatches = 0, block. Return structured remediation naming <code>/parallel-research</code>, <code>/parallel-context-build</code>, or scout-async. Explicit <code>--ack-skip-orchestration &lt;reason&gt;</code> bypass, logged for self-grading.</dd>\n      <dt>Expected outcome</dt><dd>Moves subagent adoption from 18% toward the &gt;30% target; cuts parent-context bloat (and downstream $) on the heaviest-cost session class.</dd>\n    </dl>\n  </article>\n\n  <article class=\"rec\">\n    <header class=\"rec__head\">\n      <span class=\"rec__rank\">#4</span>\n      <h3 class=\"rec__title\">Real-tool few-shot examples + batched-tool description leadership</h3>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">conf 0.80</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--high\">impact: high</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--low\">effort: low</span>\n    </header>\n    <dl class=\"rec__meta\">\n      <dt>Evidence</dt><dd>Parallel/serial ratio 0.127 despite explicit directive. Current system-prompt example uses a fictional <code>example_complex_tool</code> — models pattern-match to examples, not abstractions.</dd>\n      <dt>Action</dt><dd>(a) Replace the fake-tool example with 2–3 real-tool examples (parallel <code>Read × 3</code>; <code>Grep + find_files + Read</code>; multi-command <code>ctx_batch_execute</code>) annotated \"independent → one block.\" (b) Edit descriptions of <code>ctx_batch_execute</code>, <code>fff_multi_grep</code>, <code>web_search</code> to lead with the batch use-case. (c) Add to <code>ctx_execute</code>: \"For ≥2 independent commands, use <code>ctx_batch_execute</code> instead.\"</dd>\n      <dt>Expected outcome</dt><dd>Lift parallel/serial ratio from 0.127 toward 0.25+; cut wall-clock latency on read-heavy turns.</dd>\n    </dl>\n  </article>\n\n  <article class=\"rec\">\n    <header class=\"rec__head\">\n      <span class=\"rec__rank\">#5</span>\n      <h3 class=\"rec__title\">Verify prompt-caching is enabled on the stable system-prompt prefix</h3>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">conf 0.75</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--high\">impact: high</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--low\">effort: low</span>\n    </header>\n    <dl class=\"rec__meta\">\n      <dt>Evidence</dt><dd>The system prompt (skills + AGENTS.md + tool descriptions) is ~30 KB and identical turn-over-turn within a session. 385 sessions × multi-turn × 30 KB ≈ a meaningful share of $1,951 if not cached.</dd>\n      <dt>Action</dt><dd>Audit pi's Anthropic client wrapper for <code>cache_control: {type:'ephemeral'}</code> on the stable system-prompt block and the skills/AGENTS.md region. Add a regression test asserting prefix-hash stability across turns. If absent, enable.</dd>\n      <dt>Expected outcome</dt><dd>If currently off: ~90% cut on cached-prefix input cost — plausibly 20–40% of total $1,951. If on: confirms and closes the question.</dd>\n    </dl>\n  </article>\n\n  <article class=\"rec\">\n    <header class=\"rec__head\">\n      <span class=\"rec__rank\">#6</span>\n      <h3 class=\"rec__title\">Block interactive-TTY commands at the Bash tool boundary</h3>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">conf 0.78</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--high\">impact: high</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--low\">effort: low</span>\n    </header>\n    <dl class=\"rec__meta\">\n      <dt>Evidence</dt><dd>\"sudo: a terminal is required to read the password\" loop pattern across Bash's 271 errors (5.6% rate). The failure looks like \"no output\" rather than \"needs TTY\", so the model retries.</dd>\n      <dt>Action</dt><dd>Pre-flight Bash commands against a deny/needs-TTY list (<code>sudo</code> without <code>-n</code>, interactive <code>ssh</code>, <code>vim</code>, <code>less</code> without piping). Return a structured error naming the cause (\"requires TTY; rerun with <code>sudo -n</code> or pipe input\") instead of letting the process hang.</dd>\n      <dt>Expected outcome</dt><dd>Removes a contributor to both the 681 failed-retries and long-session tail durations.</dd>\n    </dl>\n  </article>\n\n  <article class=\"rec\">\n    <header class=\"rec__head\">\n      <span class=\"rec__rank\">#7</span>\n      <h3 class=\"rec__title\">Fuzzy-fallback Edit.oldText anchoring + stale-cache invalidation</h3>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">conf 0.82</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--high\">impact: high</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--med\">effort: medium</span>\n    </header>\n    <dl class=\"rec__meta\">\n      <dt>Evidence</dt><dd>Edit's 6.3% error rate is dominated by \"oldText not unique / not found\" — usually whitespace/CRLF drift, or anchoring against a stale Read cache after another tool mutated the file. The Read-retry-after-Edit pattern is the signature of anchor staleness.</dd>\n      <dt>Action</dt><dd>Two-tier match: exact first, then whitespace-normalized (CRLF/LF, trailing whitespace, tab/space drift). Accept only if exactly one normalized candidate; otherwise return the candidate list for disambiguation. Hook write tools to bump a per-path version counter that invalidates Read caches.</dd>\n      <dt>Expected outcome</dt><dd>Cuts Edit-retry-after-Read churn — contributor to both failed-retries (681) and dup-arg Reads (subset of 537).</dd>\n    </dl>\n  </article>\n\n  <article class=\"rec\">\n    <header class=\"rec__head\">\n      <span class=\"rec__rank\">#8</span>\n      <h3 class=\"rec__title\">Per-session cost + orchestration telemetry ledger (JSONL)</h3>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">conf 0.90</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--high\">impact: high</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--med\">effort: medium</span>\n    </header>\n    <dl class=\"rec__meta\">\n      <dt>Evidence</dt><dd>This analysis ran on aggregate-only data; per-session cost histogram, model/tier distribution, task-class breakdown, per-error-cluster counts, and per-session orchestration ratios are not in the corpus. Every recommendation below 0.85 confidence carries residual uncertainty for this reason.</dd>\n      <dt>Action</dt><dd>Cost-and-orchestration hook appending JSONL to <code>~/.pi/telemetry/{cost,orchestration}.jsonl</code>: <code>{session_id, task_class, tool, model, input_tokens, output_tokens, cached_tokens, cost_usd, ts}</code> plus per-session rollup <code>{write_n, edit_n, bash_mutate_n, subagent_n, async_n, workflow_n, ratio}</code>. Ship <code>pi cost</code> and <code>pi sessions analyze --orchestration</code> CLIs. Local-only, opt-in for upload.</dd>\n      <dt>Expected outcome</dt><dd>Converts ≥10 second-tier items from \"directional 0.55–0.75\" to measured numbers within a week of new data. Indirect impact but the highest-leverage enabler.</dd>\n    </dl>\n  </article>\n\n  <article class=\"rec\">\n    <header class=\"rec__head\">\n      <span class=\"rec__rank\">#9</span>\n      <h3 class=\"rec__title\">Hard tool-call ceiling with forced-summarization at p99 (~260 calls)</h3>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">conf 0.78</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--high\">impact: high</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--med\">effort: medium</span>\n    </header>\n    <dl class=\"rec__meta\">\n      <dt>Evidence</dt><dd>p99 = 258 tool calls; max = 414. The ~60% gap above p99 is the long tail consistent with runaway loops, not legitimately large jobs. Reinforced by failed-retry and dup-arg counts concentrating in the same sessions.</dd>\n      <dt>Action</dt><dd>Circuit-breaker at ~260 calls: inject a synthetic system turn forcing summarize-to-disk → declare remaining work as todos → hand off to a fresh-context continuation that inherits the digest. Non-destructive. Exempt sessions whose recent N calls show diverse tool/arg signatures.</dd>\n      <dt>Expected outcome</dt><dd>Bounds worst-case session $. Capping the max-414 sessions at ~260 with handoff trims ~150 calls × avg-cost from the worst sessions — disproportionate $ impact on the long-tail.</dd>\n    </dl>\n  </article>\n\n  <article class=\"rec\">\n    <header class=\"rec__head\">\n      <span class=\"rec__rank\">#10</span>\n      <h3 class=\"rec__title\">Flip <code>subagent</code> dispatch default to <code>async: true</code></h3>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--conf\">conf 0.72</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--med\">impact: medium</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge--low\">effort: low</span>\n    </header>\n    <dl class=\"rec__meta\">\n      <dt>Evidence</dt><dd>Of subagent-using sessions, only 11/18 ≈ 61% used async. ~40% of delegations block the parent despite AGENTS.md saying \"Foreground is the explicit opt-out, not the default.\" <code>workflow</code> already defaults <code>background: true</code> — precedent exists.</dd>\n      <dt>Action</dt><dd>Flip schema default of <code>async</code> in the subagent tool definition. Update the system-prompt guideline that currently says <code>async (default: false)</code>. One release of dual-default migration behind a config flag.</dd>\n      <dt>Expected outcome</dt><dd>Moves toward AGENTS.md's prescribed posture; reduces parent-session context bloat on the 40% currently blocking. Compounds with #3.</dd>\n    </dl>\n  </article>\n</section>",
        "notes": "Source: /Users/anishthite/workspace/pi-lookback/FINDINGS.md. Emitted 10 ranked recommendation cards in source order with confidence, impact, and effort badges per the ranking table."
